#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0306 expect=violation domain=DM
#note "PLAN-scalar-date-extremes (T2 review B-M2): Pool-only subject; pool P1 has TWO EX rows, (EXSTDTC 2020-01-01, EXENDTC 2020-01-05) and (EXSTDTC 2020-01-10, EXENDTC blank — an open interval); RFXENDTC 2020-01-05 -> 1 finding. missing_values=\"indeterminate\" on the per-pool EXENDTC extreme makes that pool's latest end undeterminable (the open row could end after 2020-01-05), so the EXENDTC conjunct fires on the missing answer (D34a) and the EXSTDTC conjunct fires (2020-01-10). Pins the per-pool indeterminate disposition: under skip the pool's latest end would be 2020-01-05 and the row silent."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=001
dataset DM label=Demographics
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col RFXENDTC type=Char label="Date/Time of Last Study Treatment"
---
S1 | DM | 001 | 2020-01-05
---
dataset EX class=INTERVENTIONS label="Exposure"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col POOLID  type=Char label="Pool Identifier"
col EXSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col EXTRT   type=Char label="Name of Treatment"
col EXSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Treatment"
col EXENDTC type=Char label="End Date/Time of Treatment"
---
S1 | EX |  | P1 | 1 | DRUG A | 2020-01-01 | 2020-01-05
S1 | EX |  | P1 | 2 | DRUG A | 2020-01-10 |
---
dataset POOLDEF label="Pool Definition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col POOLID  type=Char label="Pool Identifier"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
---
S1 | P1 | 001
---
